  description="The terms for using futureclaritytechnologies.com, booking a free audit, and working with FutureClarity Technologies, including how monthly plans work and how to cancel."
>
  <p>
    These terms cover futureclaritytechnologies.com and working with FutureClarity Technologies
    ("we", "us"). By using the site or booking a free audit, you agree to them. Our
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle information.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices on the site</h2>
  <p>
    The prices on this site are typical ranges to help you plan, not offers. What you pay is set in a
    written quote after your free audit, before any work starts. If something in a quote or signed
    agreement differs from these terms, the quote or agreement wins.
  </p>

  <h2>The free audit</h2>
  <p>
    The audit is free and comes with no obligation to buy anything. We may decline or reschedule an
    audit. Any audit report we send you is our honest read of what we could see at the time, based
    on public information and automated checks, which can miss things.
  </p>

  <h2>Monthly plans and cancelling</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Monthly care</strong> and <strong>pay-monthly websites</strong> are optional. If you
      choose one, your quote shows the monthly price, and the plan renews each month until you cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cancel anytime</strong> by email to <a href="mailto:beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com">beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com</a>,
      a text or call to <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>, or the same way you signed up.
      There's no cancellation fee. You won't be charged for any month after the one in which you
      cancel, and we'll confirm the cancellation in writing.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a monthly price is going to change, we'll tell you in writing at least 30 days before, so
      you can cancel first.
    </li>
    <li>
      A pay-monthly website includes hosting and edits while the plan is active. If your quote
      includes a buyout or a minimum term, it says so up front.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Texts and emails our automations send</h2>
  <p>
    Many of the workflows we build send texts or emails to your customers, such as reminders,
    review requests and missed-call replies. You're responsible for having your customers'
    permission to contact them and for following the laws that apply, such as the Telephone
    Consumer Protection Act and CAN-SPAM. We set these up with opt-outs (customers can reply STOP),
    and we'll tell you if a workflow needs consent you may not have. Texting services may also need
    your business registered with the phone carriers, which we help with.
  </p>

  <h2>Your accounts and other software</h2>
  <p>
    If you skip monthly care, we set things up on your own accounts, and you pay those services'
